---
import Accent from "@/components/landing/Accent.astro";
import Tag from "@/components/landing/Tag.astro";
import { site } from "@/site";

const source = "https://leerob.com/agents";
---

<section id="why" class="flex scroll-mt-14 flex-col gap-14 px-6 py-24 sm:px-10">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-8" data-reveal>
    <Tag>Why now</Tag>
    <p class="max-w-4xl text-[30px] font-medium leading-[1.18] tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance sm:text-[40px]">
      Teams are deleting their CMS. Orso brings <Accent>everyone else</Accent> along.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted-ink">
      Cursor moved cursor.com off its CMS and back into the repo as Markdown, and Prefect did the same. The reason
      is simple: a CMS was built for people clicking through a UI, and now most changes start with an agent.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-4 border-l-2 border-brand pl-6" data-reveal style="--d: 80ms">
    <blockquote class="text-[22px] font-medium leading-snug tracking-[-0.02em] text-balance sm:text-[26px]">
      “With AI and coding agents, the cost of an abstraction has never been higher.”
    </blockquote>
    <figcaption class="font-mono text-[12px] text-faint">
      Lee Robinson · <a class="hover:text-ink" href={source} rel="noopener">Coding Agents &amp; Complexity Budgets</a>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-3 border-t border-dashed border-hairline-strong pt-10" data-reveal>
    <p class="font-mono text-[12px] text-faint">a note from the maker</p>
    <p class="text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted-ink">
      That move works when the people editing the site already work like developers. Most marketing teams don't.
      Delete the CMS and someone still asks, the week after, “can you change the pricing?” I built Orso so they can
      do it themselves, with the forms, drafts and safe Publish button a CMS gave them, while the content stays in
      the repo. <span class="text-ink">If it isn't simple enough for my own non-technical teammates, it isn't done.</span>
    </p>
    <p class="font-mono text-[12px] text-faint">
      — Blaise · <a class="hover:text-ink" href={site.author.href} rel="noopener">{site.author.label}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
